1
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,390
you stop?

2
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:30,860
Shut it up!

3
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:35,020
This is my heart of the heart
and heart. We have their friends.

4
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:39,797
We're not there yet.

5
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:41,762
We don't have power to touch it.

6
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:45,280
We don't have power to reach out.

7
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:49,160
we're not even ready. We're not ready.

8
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:50,600
We're not ready.

9
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:51,730
We're not ready.

10
00:00:51,813 --> 00:00:52,643
We're not ready.

11
00:00:52,726 --> 00:00:53,556
I'm a complete genius,

12
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:57,980
I'm a complete genius.

13
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:05,360
Oh

14
00:01:27,980 --> 00:01:29,140
Whoa!

15
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,180
That one hurt!

16
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:49,540
It's so cold!

17
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:59,220
Thanks to the help of Gardenfall, the
god atop the clouds, we descended safely.

18
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:00,497
The north is closer!

19
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:01,410
The south is!

20
00:02:01,493 --> 00:02:02,777
You want to pull to the face?

21
00:02:02,860 --> 00:02:05,617
You need to knock your
brain around in a wet run!

22
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:07,229
That's enough of you, too.

23
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:10,720
Do you ever stop squabbling? Knock it off.

24
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,720
Now that's easy.

25
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:15,817
Our new goal will be the last
island on the Grand Line.

26
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:20,617
However, we will require copies of all
four road poneglyphs to find its location.

27
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:22,877
You mean like the one we already found?

28
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,901
There is one in the land of Wano.

29
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:27,720
Yeah, our Mokumo Dukedom has one as well.

30
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:31,340
All this time, you guys
had stones back at home!

31
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:33,257
It's different than the last one more.

32
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:34,380
It's colored red.

33
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:36,397
But that's the kind I need most!

34
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,117
You should have told me sooner!

35
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:40,197
Let's get him, then two more to go.

36
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:43,717
Well, took a little effort, but I
nabbed a rubbing of linl and stones,

37
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,237
so with your help, I'll have three.

38
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:48,197
And I have a pretty good
hunch where the fourth one is.

39
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:49,957
Nice work, Roger.

40
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:52,277
We're even closer than I realized.

41
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:54,740
Our goal is right within our grasp.

42
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:57,697
Sorry to bring the mood down.

43
00:02:57,780 --> 00:02:59,997
But I think that fall
really messed up our ship.

44
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,340
How is it?

45
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:03,657
It's hard to tell with my untrained eye.

46
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:05,497
But we're gonna need
some repairs and quick.

47
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:07,717
All right, then I know just where to go.

48
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:08,940
And where's that?

49
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:11,437
Water 7, the city of water.

50
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:12,737
And a quarter town.

51
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:13,957
Sounds romantic!

52
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,540
Full speed ahead! Let's go!

53
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:21,311
Thus, we ventured to a city of shipwrights

54
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:25,093
in order to repair the damages
to Roger's beloved vassal.

55
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:42,560
Roger, what brings you here today?

56
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:44,020
Greetings, Tom.

57
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:45,920
Hey, it's good to see you.

58
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,520
Tom, hey.

59
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:52,580
Wow, this is quite the reunion, isn't it?

60
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:54,460
Yeah, we missed you, friend.

61
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:57,729
Finished that project yet?

62
00:03:57,980 --> 00:03:59,837
You talking about the Sea Train?

63
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:00,780
You're crazy.

64
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:03,354
That thing's still in the design phase.

65
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:11,700
You're still rowdy after
all this time, I see.

66
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:20,580
You must be an orphan, huh?

67
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:23,801
I can put in a good word
with our captain for you.

68
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:27,060
You guys are pirates, right? What of it?

69
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:28,993
Then no thanks, mister.

70
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:31,437
A bunch of pirates just
dumped me off here.

71
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,460
Did they now?

72
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:35,780
Never mind then.

73
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,660
Off we go!

74
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:31,720
This is Fishman Island.

75
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:34,117
I've been here with White Kitchen.

76
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:36,560
Best not to drop your guard, everyone.

77
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:39,409
It's no less deadly
the second time around.

78
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:44,040
Hey, Rayleigh.

79
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:45,957
Did you hear someone's feet just now?

80
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:47,158
You hearing voices?

81
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:49,840
There's no one all the way down here. No.

82
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,340
I heard it too.

83
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,360
Glad I'm not alone, Odin.

84
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:56,855
But who could be calling out
to us 10,000 leagues deep?

85
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:02,240
See, Toki?

86
00:06:02,460 --> 00:06:03,900
That's Fishman Island.

87
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:05,420
How remarkable.

88
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:08,780
An entire city encased in a giant bubble.

89
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:10,160
Oh, look.

90
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:12,120
Fishman soldiers?

91
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,480
We're surrounded.

92
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:17,920
State your business, service
dwellers. Huh? Whoa, there.

93
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,757
No need to blow the man down.

94
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:21,617
Don't you recognize me, Neptune?

95
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:22,820
It's me, Roger.

96
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,230
Roger?

97
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:27,680
Ah, yes, I see now.

98
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:29,700
So you're the foretold ones.

99
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:33,225
I assure you, we're not
up to anything crooked.

100
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:36,317
A man of your stature's
scared of a little prophecy.

101
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:37,940
You're better than that.

102
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:40,057
It had cautioned us that very soon,

103
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:42,937
someone will destroy the
gates of Fishman Island.

104
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:46,520
Then suddenly you arrived,
so I'm a bit weary, you see.

105
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:48,150
Oh!

106
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:50,880
King Neptune!

107
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:52,090
It's been shattered!

108
00:06:52,173 --> 00:06:54,335
The Sea Kings are chewing up the gate!

109
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:57,220
They're too gentle to do such a thing!

110
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,440
It can't be!

111
00:06:58,940 --> 00:06:59,860
It came true.

112
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:03,557
There's a hole in the outer bubble!

113
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:05,640
Go and seal it up this instant!

114
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:08,460
So the prophecy was real.

115
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:10,620
And you nearly killed us over it!

116
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:16,015
The Sea Kings are in a restless state.

117
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:18,977
They're waiting for the
mermaid princess to be born.

118
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:19,890
Princess?

119
00:07:19,973 --> 00:07:21,517
That means there's another prophecy.

120
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:23,900
So, the king should expect a baby?

121
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:25,160
How wonderful.

122
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:26,960
Wait a moment.

123
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:29,537
I can't have a child
before I've chosen a bride.

124
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:31,020
And it's far too soon.

125
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:33,177
I only took up the
throne a few months ago.

126
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:35,084
I'd trust the prophet, my lord.

127
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:38,442
She foresaw the death of
the former king exactly.

128
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:40,149
Her track record is solid.

129
00:07:42,260 --> 00:07:44,617
And she was right about that beautiful...

130
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:46,777
Sorry, I mean that dreadful...

131
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:50,120
mermaid Otohime and her
political protest as well.

132
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:53,200
Certainly ill tidings, that one.

133
00:07:57,180 --> 00:08:01,121
Those prophecies have been riling
up our entire kingdom as of late.

134
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:02,817
While that's interesting,

135
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:06,257
we didn't come down here to
catch up on small talk, Neptune.

136
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:07,760
Oh, I nearly forgot.

137
00:08:08,940 --> 00:08:10,060
How's the progress?

138
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:14,720
Well, I presume two stones would
provide us with a clearer picture.

139
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:17,117
But it seems to be quite the opposite.

140
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:20,680
This is an apology from
someone named Joy Boy.

141
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:22,070
Incredible.

142
00:08:22,153 --> 00:08:25,120
This man can really
transcribe them? Oh, yes.

143
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:28,297
Have you heard of a weapon
that controls the Sea Kings?

144
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:29,560
A weapon, you say?

145
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:33,617
The Stone on the Sky Island said
this is where it would be located.

146
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:36,280
An ancient weapon with the name of a god.

147
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:39,434
Poseidon, it's called.

148
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:46,337
Well, truthfully, that does
line up with Charlie's prophecy.

149
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:49,655
Though the implications of
it are rather chilling, hmm?

150
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:55,160
Every few centuries, a mermaid who
can speak to sea kings is born here,

151
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:57,458
and Charlie said one is coming soon.

152
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:02,860
I fear that she will be my daughter.

153
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:07,637
Hard to believe your soon-to-be little girl
is a weapon that can destroy the world.

154
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:10,240
I'm telling myself it's just a prediction.

155
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:14,697
And obviously a deadly weapon is
only deadly if you use it as such.

156
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:18,074
Who could have guessed that
Poseidon would be a mermaid?

157
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:28,700
So, Charlie, when will this
mermaid princess be born?

158
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:36,900
This many! Huh?

159
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,146
Seems we still have a decade.

160
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:42,797
Though I must ask, why would you
take an interest in such a weapon?

161
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:44,197
I'm disappointed in you!

162
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:45,574
You're wrong, Neptune.

163
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:46,957
We're not after the weapon.

164
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:50,077
The people who left the treasure behind
were the ones who called it that.

165
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:52,513
I promise we're just after their riches.

166
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:54,713
Are you feeling better?

167
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:56,437
Rest assured, old friend,

168
00:09:56,520 --> 00:10:00,177
we will not be coming back in the future
to kidnap your hairy fish daughter.

169
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:02,200
Oh, she won't be hairy.

170
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:16,737
Gather up all of the crew.

171
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:18,877
It's time to ship up Ace's crew.

172
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:21,057
Wave goodbye but don't you cry.

173
00:10:21,140 --> 00:10:22,757
Our memories remain.

174
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:25,377
Our days are not a passing dream.

175
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:27,897
Neverlasting though they seem to be.

176
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:29,297
So who will be today?

177
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:31,357
Yet the winds are lullaby.

178
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:44,177
Yo-ho-ho-ho.

179
00:10:44,260 --> 00:10:46,180
Hey, me hearty-ups!

180
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:49,090
Good show!

181
00:10:57,280 --> 00:10:58,340
Oded! Hey!

182
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:00,820
Something wrong, Red Dorry?

183
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:03,840
I think Lady Toki is sick! Where is she?

184
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:13,577
Toki, don't you worry.

185
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:15,600
I am right here with you.

186
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:20,660
What my advice?

187
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:25,397
Toki's traveled the world with you, but
there's something that should be considered.

188
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,600
Her original destination was Wano.

189
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:30,434
I'm a bit concerned for her well-being.

190
00:11:30,620 --> 00:11:32,620
She's been at sea for a long time.

191
00:11:32,780 --> 00:11:35,000
Her fatigue is catching up with her.

192
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:36,957
I'll give it to you straight.

193
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:38,805
If she presses on, she'll die.

194
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:42,120
She ought to disembark
at Wano. Don't risk it.

195
00:11:42,320 --> 00:11:43,555
Toki is quite unwell.

196
00:11:44,060 --> 00:11:47,437
Kin'emon and the others don't know
about Toki or your children yet.

197
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:50,337
So Dogstorm and I will be
happy to accompany her.

198
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:52,217
They'll want a familiar
face or two around.

199
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:54,517
It takes time to adjust to a new home.

200
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:56,097
We'll take good care of them.

201
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:57,997
I don't want you, Gar, to worry.

202
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,240
I will stay, too.

203
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:02,910
Toki?

204
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:08,200
I've forbid it.

205
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,240
You must go.

206
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,220
Stop being foolish.

207
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,257
You're not the type of man
who would give up halfway.

208
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:15,757
Do it.

209
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:20,580
You must go on or face divorce!

210
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:33,797
These rags are not ours by choice.

211
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:38,174
We have eagerly been waiting for your
return as we have unfortunate news.

212
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:45,540
I know you left Kuri in our hands, and we
do apologize as we have tried our best.

213
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,920
However, something wicked
has taken over Wano.

214
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:49,910
One moment.

215
00:12:49,993 --> 00:12:51,480
You care for Odin, right?

216
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:53,582
Then I must implore you to stop.

217
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:55,020
Please, I beg of you.

218
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:56,580
Let him go.

219
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:58,960
Forgive me.

220
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:03,480
I am leaving again, at least for a time.

221
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:14,720
Even as I turned my back
on the land of Warnall,

222
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,765
I could tell something
about my home was amiss.

223
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:23,320
If I had stayed but a moment longer,
I knew I would never return to sea.

224
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:28,340
How could you do this, Lord Odin?

225
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:30,120
You damn jackass!

226
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:35,437
I quickly took a copy of
my country's Poneglyph and

227
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:38,755
hurried back to Roger's ship
before I could learn more.

228
00:13:39,060 --> 00:13:44,440
It was my first time home in four
years, and I only stayed mere hours.

229
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:51,360
Jackass, indeed.

230
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:54,960
Then read the cliffs yourself
if you feel that way!

231
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:58,720
Apologies, Odin. Thank you.

232
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:09,660
We then headed to Cat Viper and
Dogstorm's homeland, the Mokomo Dukedum.

233
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:13,779
A country that's carried
on the back of an elephant.

234
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:15,000
Hope this works.

235
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:18,987
They say you can only find Zoe
with the help of a beaver card.

236
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:24,210
You're right.

237
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:26,940
It's not an island, but a large Pachydon.

238
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:32,760
Who is speaking to me?

239
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:34,120
Whose voice is this?

240
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:37,300
Hey, Odin, is there
something bothering you?

241
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:39,030
Sorry.

242
00:14:39,113 --> 00:14:39,943
It's nothing really.

243
00:14:40,026 --> 00:14:41,300
Just a strange feeling.

244
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:53,258
We have received a letter
from Dogstorm and Catviper.

245
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:55,857
They survived, did they?

246
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:57,660
I assumed the worst.

247
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:01,777
It was quite the fuss when
those naughty boys went missing.

248
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:04,448
Thank you, Karoo, for
relaying this message.

249
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:13,676
There's an uneasy feeling in the air.

250
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,640
It's not like you to worry.

251
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:17,317
It must be something bad.

252
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,640
I can sense it, too.

253
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:20,333
You too, Captain Roger?

254
00:15:20,740 --> 00:15:25,387
It feels as if there's some enormous
presence and it's watching our every move.

255
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:40,980
There it is!

256
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:43,300
We found the last road, Poneglyph!

257
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:45,500
The Kozuki clan crashed!

258
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:48,329
The mink tribe are our
brethren, after all.

259
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:49,832
Just as the stories say.

260
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:56,170
Please!

261
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:57,200
I want to go!

262
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:58,500
I beg you, Karoo!

263
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:02,000
Hey, kiddo, you still
have some growing to do.

264
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:03,920
But don't worry.

265
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,060
You'll get your chance.

266
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:08,144
Just gotta wait your turn, huh?

267
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:10,180
What does that mean?

268
00:16:10,460 --> 00:16:13,100
When the time comes,
I want you to help me.

269
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:16,880
Promise I will.

270
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,864
I'll be waiting for you, Karoo.

271
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:21,040
Take care of yourself, Pedro.

272
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:26,784
Over the course of our journey,

273
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:31,020
we acquired several real pwned
lifts and all four road pwned lifts.

274
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:34,380
The end of our adventure
was drawing ever closer.

275
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,120
Captain, are you okay?

276
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:56,077
Have you boys figured out
where we're headed yet?

277
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:57,520
Yeah, good to go.

278
00:16:58,040 --> 00:16:59,640
How soon should we set out?

279
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:03,140
Immediately, of course. Yeah!

280
00:17:04,220 --> 00:17:05,180
Let's go!

281
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:14,880
Whether it was good fortune or bad,

282
00:17:15,320 --> 00:17:18,697
the apprentice Buggyiro suddenly
came down with a high fever.

283
00:17:18,780 --> 00:17:22,480
He had to stay behind and forego
the final step of the voyage.

284
00:17:22,860 --> 00:17:25,537
Don't have what it takes to make
it to the end of the trip, huh?

285
00:17:25,620 --> 00:17:26,580
What a shame.

286
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,030
FUTURE!

287
00:17:28,113 --> 00:17:30,020
I told you I'm feeling better now!

288
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:32,637
You're burning up so
much your face is red.

289
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:33,955
Just relax and sleep.

290
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:36,740
My nose is red again! I dare you!

291
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,040
I said your face!

292
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:39,630
Attaboy!

293
00:17:39,713 --> 00:17:40,659
That's the spirit!

294
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:43,360
Don't encourage those two. Come on.

295
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:48,037
All the treasure is waiting for me, Mouse!

296
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:49,740
Stop pushing yourself!

297
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:51,200
I refuse to stay here!

298
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:55,920
Please, sir!

299
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:58,340
He gotta take me with you!

300
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:02,220
Just give it up already.

301
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:03,400
You need sleep.

302
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:06,577
Despite them always being
at each other's throats,

303
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:09,484
Red Taro took it upon
himself to look after him.

304
00:18:10,820 --> 00:18:14,761
Honestly, it's hard to tell if
they're friends or enemies at times.

305
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:19,457
Please let me go with you.

306
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:20,370
I'm fine.

307
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,720
Well, we know how Buggy Giri feels.

308
00:18:24,980 --> 00:18:26,277
What's your opinion on it?

309
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:28,125
You're all right with staying.

310
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:29,430
Odin?

311
00:18:29,513 --> 00:18:30,343
Captain?

312
00:18:30,426 --> 00:18:33,977
We'll make it out there one day, but
when we do, it should be on our own ship.

313
00:18:34,060 --> 00:18:34,997
Thank

314
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:42,080
you.

315
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:13,840
It says the Roger Pirates finally did it!

316
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,353
They just made history!

317
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:18,917
That's the first time a crew traveled
all the way around the globe!

318
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,294
He's conquered it all!

319
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:21,615
The beginning to end!

320
00:19:21,860 --> 00:19:22,840
Goal Roger!

321
00:19:23,140 --> 00:19:24,200
King of the Sea!

322
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:27,240
And the King of the Pirates!

323
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:53,180
And on the day we reached that island, we
uncovered the entire truth of the world.

324
00:19:57,640 --> 00:20:00,160
We learned of the 100 year void.

325
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:04,560
We learned of the people of the
D and of the ancient weapons.

326
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:09,140
Tales from a time when the land
of Wano was open to the world.

327
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:20,537
And in the face of the treasure,
there was one thing I remember most.

328
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:24,100
All I could hear was Roger.

329
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:27,357
He just laughed.

330
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:29,997
So did we all.

331
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:35,000
On and on until tears fell from our eyes.

332
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:48,897
Oh, Joy Boy.

333
00:20:48,980 --> 00:20:49,840
Amazing.

334
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:53,996
I wish that I could have
lived in the same era as you.

335
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:59,520
This is quite the treasure
you left behind for me.

336
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:02,460
An incredible tale full of laughs.

337
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,740
Hey, everyone!

338
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:15,580
I was thinking, we're the first people
to step foot on this island in 800 years.

339
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:17,860
I think we should name it.

340
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:30,060
Love Tales!
